Yes to the first question and I am just leaving that code piece here.

load("hsPBMC")

cicero.gene_activity_matrix <- read.table("R.cicero.gene_activity_matrix.txt")
phenodata <- read.delim("cds_cell_data.txt")
featuredata <- read.delim("R.cicero.gene_activity_matrix.feature_data.txt")

featuredata$gene_rows <- featuredata$gene_short_name
row.names(featuredata) <- featuredata$gene_row

pd <- new("AnnotatedDataFrame", data = phenodata)
fd <- new("AnnotatedDataFrame", data = featuredata)

row.names(cicero.gene_activity_matrix) <- row.names(fd)
colnames(cicero.gene_activity_matrix) <- row.names(pd)

my_cds_obj <- newCellDataSet(as.matrix(cicero.gene_activity_matrix),
                       phenoData = pd, featureData = fd)

my_cds_obj <- estimateSizeFactors(my_cds_obj)

#Classify Cells

library(org.Hs.eg.db)
my_cds_obj <- classify_cells(my_cds_obj, hsPBMC,
                           db = org.Hs.eg.db,
                           cluster_extend = TRUE,
                           cds_gene_id_type = "ALIAS")

Here, I used ALIAS but both give the same error. When I ran check_markers in my cds with the marker file provided with this classifier, I got a plot where all the markers are labeled "Not in db" but I manually checked and saw that at least 5 markers are present in my cds rownames - which is weird.

